# helm walks the entire chart directory. The chart reads Chart.yaml, values.yaml,
# values.schema.json, templates/ and rules/ and nothing else (see
# templates/configmaps.yaml, whose only input is .Files.Glob over rules/), so
# everything else is excluded here.
#
# This is not tidiness. Without it helm descends into .git, .venv, docs/ and
# .superpowers/, which is where the "found symbolic link" INFO lines on every run
# came from, and a single broken symlink anywhere in the tree aborts
# `helm template` with "Error: error evaluating symlink" -- failing the render
# stage for a reason that has nothing to do with any rule.
#
# Written as an explicit exclusion list rather than `*` plus `!` exceptions
# because helm's ignore parser does not honour negation: a .helmignore of `*`
# followed by `!Chart.yaml` makes helm report "Chart.yaml file is missing"
# (verified with helm v4.2.3 against this chart).
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.helmignore
.pytest_cache/
.superpowers/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
Makefile
README.md
dashboards/
docs/
examples/
requirements.txt
scripts/
tests/
tools/
validation.yaml
